{"archetypes":[{"name":"bash-parity","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Large Python finalize/ship changes claim bash behavioral parity and status-token compatibility.","prompt_body":"Investigate whether the Python finalize, ship, merge, rebase, and CI monitor paths preserve the bash reference behavior claimed by the plan. Pay close attention to status tokens, auxiliary KV fields, skip semantics, subprocess parity tests, and branches where Python now intentionally diverges from earlier code. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"git-lifecycle","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes rebase, force-push, remote-branch, and pending CI-fix state handling across modules.","prompt_body":"Investigate git lifecycle risks around postbump rebase, force-with-lease pushes, remote branch presence checks, CI-fix rebase retries, and ship-state persistence. Look for stale ref use, unsafe fallback behavior, lost pending state, branch mismatch handling, or cases where a failed push/rebase can advance the workflow incorrectly. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"runlog-recovery","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Manifest recovery and run-log finalization are changed in several call paths with fail-closed requirements.","prompt_body":"Investigate run-log manifest recovery, final report ordering, execution-issues flushes, and larch-log commit gates across pre-push, post-merge, merge command, and teardown paths. Check whether recovery failures consistently skip writes that must be fail-closed while preserving warning-only behavior where the workflow should still complete. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"design-resume","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff changes /design routing, pause/resume sentinel placement, publish behavior, and docs describing those boundaries.","prompt_body":"Investigate the /design control-flow changes for SIMPLE sentinel writes, Step 3b finalization boundaries, pause/resume compatibility repairs, and cancel/publish stdout contracts. Check that scripts, skill docs, structural harnesses, and user-facing docs describe the same lifecycle without creating duplicate or missing completion markers. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"round-telemetry","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"New design and implement review-round timing telemetry spans shell scripts, JSON rendering, docs, and allowlists.","prompt_body":"Investigate the new round timing telemetry for implement Step 5 and design Step 3, including ledger marks, round-start files, JSON report attachment, de-duplication, and pause publish cleanup of stale timing reports. Check whether timing data can be lost, attached to the wrong step interval, duplicated across resumes, or leaked through artifact allowlists. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"shell-portability","focus_area":"code-quality","weight":1,"rationale":"Many Bash changes affect harnesses and runtime scripts that must remain robust under repo shell conventions.","prompt_body":"Investigate the changed Bash scripts and harnesses for portability, quoting, set -e interactions, temp-file cleanup, jq and command absence handling, and stdout versus stderr separation. Pay particular attention to new loops, arithmetic, glob cleanup, sourced helper contracts, and whether tests accidentally depend on local environment details. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
